TI  - Interventional bronchoscopy for HPV 16 and 66 with the use of spraying 
      interferon-α (2b) plus bevacizumab and anti-reflux agent.
PG  - 101398
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2021.101398 [doi]
LID - 101398
AB  - A fifty year old male was diagnosed with bronchial HPV. He was treated with local 
      interventional treatment argon plasma coagulation and subcutaneous injections 
      bevacizumab. Spraying of the regions followed with a specially designed catheter 
      with interferon-α (2b). Systematic treatment of esomeprazole was also 
      administered. After six months the patient is disease free and on close 
      follow-up.
