TI  - A Rare Cause of Hemoptysis in Childhood: Tracheal Capillary Hemangioma.
PG  - 131-133
LID - 10.5152/TurkThoracJ.2017.16005 [doi]
AB  - Hemangiomas are benign tumors most frequently seen in childhood and are mostly 
      associated with cutaneous and mucosal surfaces. Tracheal capillary hemangiomas 
      are extremely rare. The most common presenting symptom is hemoptysis, ranging 
      from minor to major and chronic cough. We present the case of a 12-year-old boy 
      with recurrent hemoptysis due to tracheal capillary hemangioma, who was treated 
      with interventional bronchoscopy.
