TI  - Tracheal Lobular Capillary Haemangioma: A Rare Benign Cause of Recurrent 
      Haemoptysis.
PG  - 6290424
LID - 6290424
AB  - Lobular capillary haemangioma (LCH), previously known as pyogenic granuloma, is a 
      benign vascular lesion commonly found within the oral and nasal cavity. However, 
      it is rarely encountered within the trachea, where presenting features include 
      recurrent haemoptysis, cough, and wheeze. We here describe a case of a 7 mm 
      tracheal LCH in a 56-year-old woman, which was successfully resected at 
      interventional bronchoscopy using biopsy forceps. Clinicians should be aware of 
      tracheal LCH in the differential diagnosis for recurrent haemoptysis.
